Package { #name : 'Aconcagua-Arithmetic-GS64-Base-Extensions', #comment : 'GS64''s Number hierarchy features rigid object comparison logic. Type coercion is only attempted if the target object responds to _isNumber with true. However, because _isNumber is an inlined method, it cannot be overridden in custom classes. We need to slightly patch these comparison methods to allow symmetric evaluation between standard numbers and arithmetic formulas that yield numeric values.' }
